{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And the hare.</b> The reason the species is mentioned in feminine language is that the dimension of impurity is at times such that the female is superior to the male, and the male is subordinate to her — and the female is remembered for the very reason that the male is always mentioned and not the female, for she is the principal. And you will find that they said in the Zohar (Pinḥas 231a) in the sod of the liver's lobe, that the female gives a lobe to the male; and we have already written that every forbidden species is an aspect of the kelipah stripped of life and of good."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:55:13.112925180Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}